/*
 * src/criware_data.c
 * Data-only C translation unit for the CriWare SDK retail data sections.
 * Replaces the generated assembly dump build/us/asm/criware_data.s.
 * Verified byte-for-byte / reloc-for-reloc against
 * build/us/obj/criware_data.o via tools/coop/lib/data_match.py.
 *
 *   .rodata 0x7D18 bytes  .data 0x8F0C bytes  .bss 0x3A730 bytes
 *
 * Generated by .scratch/gen_criware_data.py; hand-typed where the
 * retail data is identifiable (strings, float tables, message
 * structs, function-pointer tables).
 *
 * Notes on the emission scheme:
 *  - Written in C (not C++): MWCC only folds (unsigned int)fn + off
 *    pointer relocations into static .rela entries in C mode; C++ mode
 *    routes them through a runtime __sinit__ stub, which would add .text.
 *  - MWCC emits per-symbol relocations in REVERSE order while the
 *    retail splitter's .rela lists are forward-by-offset, so symbols
 *    with >= 2 relocations are split into one 4-byte global per word
 *    (the first word keeps the retail symbol name).
 *  - .bss symbols are declared in reverse address order (MWCC emits
 *    .bss in reverse declaration order).
 */

